# PAGE-KEYS-SETTINGS-COLUMN round 3: where the four lists fx hangs under the
# composer start (projectedAnchorColumn, visual_layout.zig:705-713; the
# anchors, input_presentation.zig:356-363, :383-386@481104fd). The model,
# provider and file lists anchor at their argument while the caret is on its
# row, else at the start of the caret's row; the slash menu of commands and
# skills has no anchor (slashRawAnchor, :287-292: no argument completion) and
# starts at column 1. At 60 columns a row holds 58 cells: each list once on a
# one-row composer, then under a token longer than a row, which starts on the
# first row and breaks onto the second, where the caret is; the slash word
# then with the caret moved up a row. No typed text starts with `-`, which
# tmux would read as a flag. Run it at 24x60: at 120 columns every token
# fits its row and the `-wrapped` snaps are one-row ones. (A `resize 24x60`
# first would not do: from a wider launch fx clears the screen and writes
# its document again at the top, xfx keeps its band at the bottom -- the
# ledger's `resize-document-repaint` -- so every row would differ.) The
# provider query is `q`, which no provider matches, so the one-row list is
# its status row on both sides and not the two products' provider sets.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
work p5-page-keys-anchor-ws
models p5-page-keys-anchor-models.json
wait 4
xfx: wait 1
type /model xai/gr
wait 1
snap model-one
key C-u
wait 0.5
type /model fake/a-model-id-long-enough-to-wrap-the-composer-row-at-sixty-c
wait 1
snap model-wrapped
cursor model-wrapped
key C-u
wait 0.5
type /provider q
wait 1
snap provider-one
type a-provider-name-long-enough-to-wrap-the-composer-row-at-sixty
wait 1
snap provider-wrapped
cursor provider-wrapped
key C-u
wait 0.5
type see @a-fi
wait 1.5
snap file-one
type le-name-long-enough-to-wrap-the-composer-row-at-sixty-c
wait 1.5
snap file-wrapped
cursor file-wrapped
key C-u
wait 0.5
type /wrap-th
wait 1
snap slash-one
type e-composer-past-its-first-row-and-on-to-the-next-row-
wait 1
snap slash-wrapped
cursor slash-wrapped
key Up
wait 0.5
snap slash-wrapped-up
cursor slash-wrapped-up
